        {
          "say": "What is the difference between gross pay and net pay?",
          "reply": "**Gross pay** is the total amount earned before any deductions — your basic salary plus any allowances, overtime, or other earnings for the period. **Net pay** is what actually reaches you after deductions are taken out. Typical deductions include: - Income tax / PAYE\n- Social insurance contributions\n- Any other statutory or company deductions\n- Loan or advance installments, if applicable So the relationship is: **Net pay = Gross pay − total deductions** A simple way to picture it: gross is the figure agreed for your work, net is the figure that lands in your bank account. Your payslip normally shows both, with the deduction lines listed in between so you can see exactly what was subtracted. If you'd like, I can walk you through the specific lines on your own payslip so you can see how gross becomes net in your case.",
